        "id": "budgets",
        "title": "17. Stopping rules, latency and cost",
        "stage": "advanced",
        "takeaway": "Define budgets for proposals, tool calls, elapsed time and provider usage. Stop with an honest outcome when the task is complete, blocked or out of budget.",
        "sections": [
          {
            "title": "Understand the idea",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Define budgets for proposals, tool calls, elapsed time and provider usage. Stop with an honest outcome when the task is complete, blocked or out of budget.",
              "A maximum step count prevents an endless sequence of model decisions but does not bound one hanging tool call. A deadline needs enforcement in the executor and cancellation semantics. Token and monetary costs depend on provider usage and configuration; avoid estimating exact bills from character counts. Measure end-to-end latency, including tool and queue time."
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Work through the example",
            "paragraphs": [
              "Read this as an explicit scenario or a small local example. Identify the decision, the trusted application check and the observable result before continuing."
            ],
            "example": "Example policy, chosen for this task:\nmaximum 4 proposals\nmaximum 2 read calls\ndeadline enforced by real adapters\nstop on completed / needs_input / denied / failed / exhausted\nRepeated identical search with no new evidence -> consider stop\nThese are design choices, not universal recommended numbers."
          },
          {
            "title": "Failures and tradeoffs",
            "paragraphs": [
              "A model instruction saying stop after four steps is not an enforced counter. Parallel calls may reduce elapsed time but increase total usage and peak load. If a tool cannot be cancelled, do not claim a deadline undoes its effects. The offline workshop enforces proposal count only; it has no network or live token accounting."
            ]
          }
        ],
